### Claimed evidence
- GUARD IS `k == 1`, NOT `max == 0`. Oracle `./test12_executable 1e-8 0 0` -> full line `0 1 5e-09 0 1 1e-08 0 0 0 1 2.99e-09 -1.47e-09 6.15e-09`, i.e. cmyk = `0 0 0 1`. Here max = 1e-8f which is NOT zero, but 1e-8 < 2^-25 = 2.98023224e-8 so fl(1.0f - 1e-8f) == 1.0f exactly. A `max == 0` guard would take the else branch and divide by (1 - k) == 0, printing `-nan -nan -nan 1`. A whole-corpus sweep gives the `max == 0` guard 1436/42053 + 2558/60053 + 18966/60000 + 182/2197 mismatches.
- GUARD BOUNDARY IS EXACTLY THE 2^-25 ROUNDING THRESHOLD OF `1.0f - max`, confirming the guard tests k and not max. `2.98023224e-08 0 0` -> cmyk `0 0 0 1` (guard fires, max just below 2^-25); `3.1e-8 0 0` -> cmyk `0 1 1 1` (guard does not fire); `2.98023259e-08 0 0` -> cmyk `0 1 1 1`.
- DENOMINATOR IS `1.0f - k`, NOT `max`. For `3.1e-8 0 0`: k = fl(1-3.1e-8) = 1 - 2^-24, so 1-k = 2^-24 = 5.96046e-8, while max = 3.1e-8. Oracle m = 1 (== (1-0-k)/(1-k) = 2^-24/2^-24). Dividing the same numerator by max would give 1.92273. Variant `(1-x-k)/max` scores 9583/42053 mismatches.
- NUMERATOR IS `((1.0f - x) - k)`, NOT `(1.0f - (x + k))`. Oracle `1e30 1 1` -> cmyk `0 1 1 -1e+30`. Left-to-right: fl(1-1e30) = -1e30 = k... c numerator = fl(fl(1-1e30) - (-1e30)) = 0 exactly -> c = 0. The `(1 - (r + k))` grouping computes fl(1e30 + (-1e30)) = 0, then 1 - 0 = 1, /1e30 -> c = 1e-30. Oracle prints `0`. Variant scores 4051/42053 + 5728/60053 mismatches.
- IT IS NOT `(max - x) / max` (algebraically identical, different rounding). Oracle `1e-7 1e-8 1e-9` -> cmyk `0 1 1 1`. `(max-x)/max` gives `0 0.9 0.99 1`. Also `-3.35152436e-07 -3.35152436e-07 3.90766019e-07` -> oracle c = 1.85714 vs 1.85768; `3.90309324e-05 1.92430543e-05 3.90309324e-05` -> oracle m = 0.50687 vs 0.506979. Variant scores 10960/42053 + 15011/60053 + 13015/60000 mismatches.
- IT IS A DIVISION, NOT A MULTIPLY BY A PRECOMPUTED RECIPROCAL `inv = 1.0f/(1.0f-k)`. Oracle `0.970731616 0.244352102 0.794469595` -> cmyk `0 0.74828 0.181576 0.0292684`; the reciprocal form gives m = 0.748281. Also `0.753457367 0.707162499 0.350718945` -> oracle y = 0.534521 vs 0.53452; `0.444679856 0.123074703 0.873846352` -> oracle c = 0.491124 vs 0.491123. Variant scores 415/42053 + 598/60053 + 166/60000 mismatches.
- NO DOUBLE INTERMEDIATES IN THE CHANNELS. Full-double `(float)((1.0 - (double)x - (double)k)/(1.0 - (double)k))` is killed by `3.1e-8 0 0`: oracle c = 0, double version c = 0.479906; and by `2.98023259e-08 0 0`: oracle 0, double 0.5. Score 13819/42053 + 19160/60053. Mixed float-numerator/double-denominator is killed by `3.09588604e-19 24461076 -1.63573056e+17` -> oracle cmyk `1 0 6.68708e+09 -2.44611e+07`, mixed gives y = 6.68707e+09 (verified by direct re-invocation of the oracle), and by `-6.96511802e+23 1.6032001e-19 136639664` -> oracle c = 5.09744e+15 vs 5.09743e+15. Long-double version scores 13977/42053.
- IT IS NOT `((1.0f - k) - x) / (1.0f - k)`. `3.1e-8 0 0` -> oracle c = 0, that form gives 0.479906; `1e-7 1e-8 1e-9` -> oracle `0 1 1 1`, that form gives `0.161139 0.916114 0.991611 1`. Score 13309/42053 + 18396/60053 + 14639/60000.
- IT IS NOT `1.0f - x/max`. `inf 0.2 0.3` -> oracle cmyk `-nan -nan -nan -inf`; `1 - x/max` gives `-nan 1 1 -inf`. Score 14222/42053 + 19749/60053.
